line	<str>Attack Sir Mordred. He cannot be safespotted, but he can be flinched using the stairs (position him on the square left of the stairs whilst flinching from the square north-east of him). He can also be killed with rings of recoil or by another account poisoning and attacking right before his death.</str>
line	
line	<str>When Sir Mordred reaches 0 hitpoints, Morgan Le Faye will appear and ask that you spare him. Spare his life to discover how to save Merlin. red|Warning: Do not interrupt the dialogue or you will have to fight Sir Mordred again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the candle-maker in Catherby.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him again for a black candle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to The Lady of the Lake south-east of Taverley on the peninsula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Port Sarim. (Make sure you have bread in your inventory.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the jewellery shop to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the beggar your bread. Finish the conversation.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Zamorakian temple in the south-east corner of Varrock.</str>
line	
line	<str>Check the Chaos Altar's inscription.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Camelot with a tinderbox and enter the castle gates.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the ritual site at the north-east corner of the Camelot castle grounds (a red star in the middle of 8 columns).</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand on the star and light the black candle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Drop the bat bones on the star.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>The magic words are "Snarthon Candtrick Termanto".</col>
